  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "Losing trades clustered into two primary failure modes: intraday whipsaws on high-beta cyclical names (TATASTEEL hitting the 0.70% stop-loss almost immediately at 10:35 and 10:25) and late-session/mid-day momentum decay resulting in EOD square-offs or breakeven stops where positive gross P&L was flipped negative by transaction fees (~\u20b94.00 per trade). Furthermore, an overly ambitious 1.25% target forced winners to stay open through the afternoon liquidity trough, turning profitable mid-day excursions into scratch losses after brokerage and statutory charges.",
    "learning": "In NSE cash equities on micro-capital accounts, transaction cost drag (~0.14% round-trip) severely penalizes stagnant mid-day entries and wide targets that fail to clear before EOD; filtering out noise requires a higher volume sweep threshold (2.85x), slightly wider stop cushioning (0.75%) to survive morning volatility spikes, and a realistic target (1.10%) paired with an earlier breakeven trigger (0.85R) to lock in net profits above the fee hurdle.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.1,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.85,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 0.85,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.75
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #38 Quantitative Review & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash achieved a positive expectancy (PF: 1.38, Win Rate: 50.0%, Net P&L: \u20b9+30.55), vastly outperforming the Phase 1 zero-AI baseline. However, forensic analysis of the 6 losing trades revealed severe fee drag (\u20b944.06 total fees vs \u20b930.55 net profit), where two grossly profitable trades (`ICICIBANK` and `TATASTEEL`) flipped into net losses upon trailing stop or EOD square-off, alongside rapid 5-minute stop-outs in `TATASTEEL` during morning chop. To mitigate these microstructure frictions, we are widening `min_sl_pct` to `0.75%` to absorb high-beta morning volatility, increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to `2.85x` to demand stronger institutional participation on breakouts, tightening `min_target_pct` to `1.10%` to capture intraday moves before afternoon stagnation forces EOD exits, and lowering `breakeven_trigger_r` to `0.85R` to protect capital earlier against reversals."
